  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0 - UserFriendlyIds is now Idora.NET.\n\n      This is the UserFriendlyIds 1.1.0 feature set under a new name, as part of the Idora family of\n      identically behaving packages for .NET, JavaScript/TypeScript, Java, Go and Rust. Identifiers\n      are byte-for-byte the same format, so existing stored IDs remain valid.\n\n      Breaking renames, all mechanical:\n\n      * Package: UserFriendlyIds -> Idora.NET. Namespace and assembly: UserFriendlyIds -> Idora.\n      * services.AddUserFriendlyIds(...) -> services.AddIdora(...).\n      * IUserFriendlyIdGenerator -> IIdoraGenerator; UserFriendlyIdGenerator -> IdoraGenerator.\n      * UserFriendlyIdOptions -> IdoraOptions; UserFriendlyIdsException -> IdoraException.\n\n      Everything else - EntityPrefixAttribute, IEntityPrefixRegistry, IdGenerationStrategy and the\n      other exception types - keeps its name and behaviour.",
